    "latency_hours": "Typical hours after cycle time until the LAST lead the Day-1 window needs (f15 of the 12z) is published, measured from real Last-Modified headers on 2026-09-22 plus ~0.25h margin: HRRR 1.2h, RRFS 2.4h, REFS 2.6h. Only used to EMULATE the live member mix during historical capture (members.resolve_plan emulate_live_at); live runs check the real .idx.",
    "archive_url": "A source may set archive_url: live runs read url and historical capture reads archive_url (use it when the archive copy lags the live feed). No current source uses it. The NAM 3km nest, the one that did (AWS copy ~12h late), was removed in 2026-10 ahead of NOAA retiring NAM; its replacements are the RRFS members and the REFS ensprod track. HiResW (ARW, FV3, ARW-mem2) and HREF were removed in 2026-10 as well, when NOAA retired NAM, SREF, HREF and HiResW together; that also ended the forward-only NOMADS capture, so every remaining source (HRRR, RRFS, REFS) is archived and can be backfilled.",
    "live_run_offset_hours": "The ensemble step runs from scripts/ensemble_12z.sh (cron 15:00Z) - about anchor+3h, the same effective time it had when it ran after DailyForecast in scripts/forecasts.sh (then cron 14:30Z). The daily forecast now starts about 13:15Z, so the ensemble is a separate job."
